SEPARATE QUEUE-124 (re-referee, lock hold not shown) plain=0 salt-diet=0 total=0
SEPARATE EXIT-FORCED-AFTER-LANDING (judged at HEAD) plain=0 salt-diet=0 total=0 []
LIMITS (declared; printed by classify_cell.py --limits and beside every result table):
  - [design §D4] Every pointer the referee passes is a per-task CONSTANT (same address on every input, 64-byte aligned; the cell's tools/frame.py states it). A plain routine that ignores its pointer arguments, or whose misaligned-head path is wrong, is ACCEPTED; the first is REJECTED at TARGET on salt-diet, so the primary pair is biased toward PLAIN by exactly this class. The remedy (a per-frame window offset in frame.py, identical in both executors) is a referee change named for the n = 3 run.
  - [design §D4] Reads are observed by nothing. Neither executor nor the Target sees a read outside the declared regions: a routine whose over-read does not reach its result is ACCEPTED on both arms. Two cards admit a bounded over-read by contract.
  - [design §D4] Footprint checks are final-state. A write outside the footprint that is undone before the return is ACCEPTED on both arms.
  - [design §D4] A spec that transcribes the routine reaches TARGET and scores N/N, and no battery row detects it (full agreement means only not refuted). Its detector, the kernel-equality spec method, is owed (§D7).
  - [design §D4] tests=FAIL(native-crash) is REJECTED whatever killed the native executor; the kill's rc is in the record's tail and is not read.
  - [classifier] PASS + DISAGREE reads UNSCORABLE, as registered (§D2). The G-battery showed a routine reading an uninitialised callee-saved register reads PASS with DISAGREE on every input, so this class can hold a routine defect outside both primary denominators. It is COUNTED SEPARATELY beside the table (SEPARATE PASS+DISAGREE). The two-seed probe (n = 1) found that member's disagreement the routine's; a REJECTED reading waits on a later addendum with that evidence.
  - [design §D4] The call frame has three BLIND SPOTS: unused argument registers are always 0, the two executors start callee-saved registers differently, and NULL is never passed. A defect that lives only in one of them is ACCEPTED; the remedy (frame noise) is a referee change named for the n = 3 run.
  - [harvest] A re-referee 124 reads the TREE's only when the fleet lock log shows its build held the lock for >= the bound - 60 s; every other 124 is the queue's (UNSCORABLE), COUNTED SEPARATELY (SEPARATE QUEUE-124). A tree that hangs while the box is busy is therefore UNSCORABLE, never REJECTED: the bias runs against neither arm by construction, but it shrinks the scored n.
  - [classifier] POKED-OUT and STALLED are filed as the harness's halts of the subject; no instrument tell for either exists yet.
  - [classifier] The x86 record only. The Rust (v3) referee's classes and the agy launcher's end tokens are not mapped (they REFUSE).
  - [harvest] Uncommitted work at the end is NOT MEASURED by the harvest (no worktree is read: S2); the column prints '-'. The watcher's own `dirty N` from its SNAPSHOT line rides in the pin column.
